        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON ASSOCIATION. THE CHAMPIONSHIP.</p>
        <p>The final in the Warrington and District Bowling Association was played on the Cemetery Hotel Green on Saturday, between the Bull's Head and Rylands' team. The match was a very close one, Bull's Head ultimately winning by 20 points. Scores : BULL'S HEAD. RYLAND'S'. G Shaw J Swanton T Hackett J Berry 2l NV Roughley 2O A Gleave (captain) 11 Fairbrother lO la Wells 2l J Gleave J Jolley NV Andrews l2 W Cotta= 2l R Roberts H Williams l7 G Shaw 2l H 14'ogg 2l. J Woods ...... ........... 17</p>
        <p>Total 017 Total 197 Majority for Bull's Head 20 points. At the conclusion of the match, the Slayor (Alderman Smethurst) presented the cop to Mr. A. Weave, the captain of the Bull's Head team, and he congratulated the club on their success. WORKS ASSOCIATION HANDICAP.</p>
