      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-09-12_WidnesExaminer_art0123" n="art0123">
        <head>FRIENDLY AIATC:i.</head>
        <p>FRIENDLY AIATC:i.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON "A" V. SEEDLEY HORNETS.—The season at Wilderspool opened on Saturday, when an attendance of 3,003 assembled to witness the Combina- tion team meet Seedley Hornets, a side who played a prominent part in one of the competitions in the Manchester district last season. Interest was centred in the first appearance of a Welsh threaquarter named Harris' from Blienavon, who has a capital reputation in the Welsh district amongst the junior organizations. Young :Mclntyre, of Stockton Heath, made his debut under the professional trainer, and a strapping forward in Chesters also made a favourable impression. The visitors, however, proved no match for the " Wire- pullers," who, after starting in quite scratchy style, soon warmed to their work, and practically scored at their leisure. Cartwright raced over for a good try, which the , scorer also improved upon. Gregory reduced some of the leeway when he kicked a penalty goal for the Hornets. Daintith and Kave opened out the game towards the right wing, and Harris, taking a pass in clean fashion, scored a really good try, Kayo goaling. Seedley fell away at this period and Warrington, forcing matters, Daintith scored twice in quick succession, and added a goal, the score in favour of Warrington at the interval being eighteen points against two. The second half had not been long in progress before the Warrington backs got under weigh, and Landor scored at the corner. The pressure was maintained and Kaye scored rather cleverly, whilst a moment later the Hornets' full-back failed to make the ball dead and Cheaters dashed up to score a try. Harris next had an easy journey from a pass by Cartwright, and this was followed by Bradshaw completing a try which Harmer improved. The con- cluding try was scored by Daintith, which Cartwright converted and the final aggregate was as follows : Warrington, five goals ten tries (43 points) ; Seedley Hornets, one penalty goal (two points).</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-09-12_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <head>NORTHERN RUGBY UNION.</head>
        <p>NORTHERN RUGBY UNION.</p>
        <p>Meeting of The General Committee.</p>
        <p>A meeting of the General Committee of the Northern Union was held in Manchester on Tuesday evening. A grant of LGO was made to the Yorkshire County in aid of junior and intermediate football, and En was also granted to the Cumberland County Football Union. The following important resolution was passed, viz. : "That the laws now in force in the Northern Union League with reference to the transfer of players shall apply to the clubs in membership with or playing under the auspices of the New South Wales League, and no player shall in any circumstances transfer his services during the progress of the tour."</p>
